ACCESSIBILITY
================================================================================

Keyboard Navigation:
- All interactive elements fully keyboard accessible
- Tab order follows logical flow
- Focus states highly visible (2px mauve ring)
- Button includes aria-label
- Form inputs have proper labels (sr-only for visual design)

Screen Readers:
- Semantic HTML (form, label, button elements)
- aria-required on required inputs
- aria-describedby linking helper text to input
- role="alert" + aria-live="polite" on error messages
- sr-only labels for inputs (visually hidden, screen reader visible)

Reduced Motion Support:
- Detects prefers-reduced-motion media query
- Disables breathing animation completely
- Stops RAF animation loop (instant cursor following if motion reduced)
- Falls back to static opacity on light layers
- All transitions/animations respect user preference via CSS

Color Contrast:
- White text on dark backgrounds (high contrast)
- Mauve button text uses dark background for readability
- Focus rings use sufficient opacity for visibility
- Error states use sufficient saturation

