THE UNEXPECTED - "OH!" MOMENT
================================================================================

Cast Shadow When Light Passes Behind Card:

Physics:
- Calculates if light is in "behind zone" (expanded card bounds)
- Shadow offset inversely proportional to light position
- Shadow moves OPPOSITE to light direction (correct physics)
- Formula: offset = (cardCenter - lightPos) * 0.02

Visual Treatment:
- Soft black shadow (blur: 40px)
- Opacity tied to scatterFactor (0-0.4 max)
- Smooth opacity transition (0.6s cubic-bezier)
- Transform transition (0.3s) follows light movement
- z-index: -1 renders behind card

Why It's Unexpected:
- Reverses typical expectation (light usually in front)
- Creates spatial depth perception
- Physically accurate (not decorative)
- Subtle - only visible when light is near and behind
- Makes card feel three-dimensional in space
- "Oh!" realization: the light has volume and position

Bonus Delight:
- Button flash creates brief light flare on submit
- Feels responsive and satisfying
- Synchronized across all light layers

